Notes on how it's wired up:

- `onBack` and `onPay` are the only integration points — plug `onBack` into your router/screen-stack pop, and `onPay(address)` into your order-creation call (e.g. `Telegram.WebApp.openInvoice(...)` or your backend's checkout endpoint).
- CSS uses `--tg-theme-*` custom properties with fallbacks, so it automatically matches the user's Telegram theme (light/dark) when those variables are set on `:root` via `Telegram.WebApp.themeParams`, but still looks correct standalone.
- Validation is inline (name, phone, city, street, postal code required; apartment and comment optional) and runs on blur and on submit.
- The Pay button disables while `isSubmitting` is true or the cart is empty, and shows the computed total.
